        "id": "1",
        "title": "Planning a Small Birthday Celebration ",
        "body": "Dear Neighbors,${NL}I’m excited to propose a community garden project for our block and would love your feedback! After months of research, I’ve secured a vacant lot on Elm Street, available starting June 1st, for us to transform into a shared green space. The goal is to grow fresh produce—like tomatoes, herbs, and squash—while fostering a sense of community. The city has agreed to waive the permit fees if we commit to maintaining it, but we’ll need to fund tools, seeds, and irrigation ourselves. I estimate $800 to start—would a crowdfunding campaign work, or should we seek a local sponsor?${NL}I envision raised garden beds to accommodate all skill levels, plus a compost system to keep it sustainable. Should we limit plots to one per household, or allow multiple based on interest? I’d also like to host a kickoff event—perhaps a planting day with refreshments. Would you prefer mid-June or early July, considering summer schedules? Finally, I could use volunteers to clear weeds and prep the soil on May 25th from 9 a.m. to noon. Please reply by May 15th with your thoughts—I’d hate to move forward without everyone’s input!${NL}Best regards,${NL}Lila (Unit 12B)${NL}",
